  {
   "@id": "publication/2010_Guidi_Performance",
   "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
   "identifier": "2010_Guidi_Performance",
   "name": "Performance Evaluation of Triangulation Based Range Sensors",
   "datePublished": "2010",
   "kg:publicationType": "Journal article",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/guidi-gabriele"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/magrassi-grazia"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/bordegoni-monica"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "The performance of 2D digital imaging systems depends on several factors related with both optical and electronic processing. These concepts have originated standards, which have been conceived for photographic equipment and bi-dimensional scanning systems, and which have been aimed at estimating different parameters such as resolution, noise or dynamic range. Conversely, no standard test protocols currently exist for evaluating the corresponding performances of 3D imaging systems such as laser scanners or pattern projection range cameras. This paper is focused on investigating experimental processes for evaluating some critical parameters of 3D equipment, by extending the concepts defined by the ISO standards to the 3D domain. The experimental part of this work concerns the characterization of different range sensors through the extraction of their resolution, accuracy and uncertainty from sets of 3D data acquisitions of specifically designed test objects whose geometrical characteristics are known in advance. The major objective of this contribution is to suggest an easy characterization process for generating a reliable comparison between the performances of different range sensors and to check if a specific piece of equipment is compliant with the expected characteristics.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "7192-7215",
   "issn": "1424-8220",
   "url": "https://doi.org/10.3390/s100807192",
   "volumeNumber": "10",
   "issueNumber": "8",
   "sameAs": [
    "https://doi.org/10.3390/s100807192",
    "https://iris.uniroma1.it/handle/11573/905440"
   ],
   "kg:scopusId": "2-s2.0-77957226974",
   "kg:wosId": "000281481000010",
   "kg:openAccess": "yes",
   "kg:anvurScientificArea08": "yes",
   "kg:anvurClassA": "no",
   "isPartOf": {
    "@id": "venue/sensors"
   },
   "about": [
    {
     "@id": "keyword/3d-laser-scanning"
    },
    {
     "@id": "keyword/sensor-integration"
    }
   ],
   "kg:caseStudyScale": [
    {
     "@id": "scale/not-applicable"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "publication/2009_Guidi_Diachronic",
   "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
   "identifier": "2009_Guidi_Diachronic",
   "name": "Diachronic representation of ancient buildings: studies on the “San Giovanni in Conca” Basilica in Milan",
   "datePublished": "2009",
   "kg:publicationType": "Journal article",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/guidi-gabriele"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "Questo articolo propone una metodologia per la rappresentazione virtuale di Beni Culturali non più esistenti, che integra l’acquisizione dello stato di fatto attraverso le tecniche di rilievo 3D digitale, con l'analisi delle fonti storiche, letterarie, catastali ed iconografiche. L’uso del dato geometrico oggettivo come griglia interpretativa di partenza consente di costruire un metodo scalabile e riapplicabile su diversi manufatti. Il processo è qui sperimentato con la ricostruzione virtuale delle fasi evolutive di una chiesa emblematica per la sua storia tormentata: la Basilica di San Giovanni in Conca a Milano. Attraverso tale ricostruzione viene proposta una rappresentazione realistica e comprensibile delle storia del manufatto, utile sia per l’analisi critica degli studiosi che per la valorizzazione turistica.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "69-80",
   "issn": "1828-5961",
   "url": "https://doi.org/10.6092/issn.1828-5961/1799",
   "volumeNumber": "2",
   "issueNumber": "4",
   "sameAs": [
    "https://doi.org/10.6092/issn.1828-5961/1799",
    "https://iris.uniroma1.it/handle/11573/905436"
   ],
   "kg:wosId": "000219852800007",
   "kg:openAccess": "yes",
   "kg:anvurScientificArea08": "yes",
   "kg:anvurClassA": "no",
