  {
   "@id": "publication/2019_Russo_CurveGenerative",
   "@type": "Chapter",
   "identifier": "2019_Russo_CurveGenerative",
   "name": "Il ruolo delle curve generative nel Design Nautico",
   "datePublished": "2019",
   "kg:publicationType": "Book chapter",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "In the Industrial Design field, the translation of an idea into its realization may be represented by shape research and analysis, a complex mediation process between tradition and innovation, significance and meaning, design freedom and material constraint. In this iterative refining process, curves represent the generative starting point for the construction of complex, liquid surfaces. A significant role in this field is held by nautical design, a complex discipline in which the geometric construction and representation activity assumes a key role in the graphic restitution of complex spatial shapes defined by curve networks. The discussion analyses the role of the curve in Nautical Design from the constructive and formal genesis of boats, exploring curve typologies and their geometry evolution in Industrial Design. Starting from the dichotomy between new project and real object, the contribution highlights and compares the use of project curves versus sections extracted from three-dimensional models obtained through a Reverse Modeling process.",
   "inLanguage": "ITA",
   "pagination": "197-210",
   "isbn": "9788891794000",
   "publisher": "FrancoAngeli",
   "url": "http://ojs.francoangeli.it/_omp/index.php/oa/catalog/book/409",
