  {
   "@id": "publication/2026_Ulivieri_VeronaScholl",
   "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
   "identifier": "2026_Ulivieri_VeronaScholl",
   "name": "Critical comparison of von Sholl's never-built plans for the Verona bridgehead",
   "datePublished": "2026",
   "kg:publicationType": "Conference paper",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/ulivieri-denise"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "'Verona is the centre of gravity of Austrian rule in Italy' and served as the main stronghold of the Quadrilateral, a fortification system built between 1831-1866. Field Marshal Radetzky and engineer Franz von Sholl proposed multiple plans to reinforce the city with entrenchments along the Adige River, forming a bridgehead. Von Sholl developed several hypotheses, with his 1834-38 design representing an ambitious project that was largely unrealized. Between 1850-1852, followers constructed a single isolated fort based on his earlier concepts. This research examines von Sholl's various bridgehead proposals, comparing them with what was actually built and what remains today, offering insights into the strategic logic of this Austrian fortification system.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "225-232",
   "isbn": "9788893774345",
   "publisher": "Sapienza Università Editrice / edUPV",
   "url": "https://ocs.editorial.upv.es/index.php/FORTMED/FORTMED2026/paper/view/21376",
   "sameAs": [
    "https://doi.org/10.4995/Fortmed2026.2026.21376",
    "https://iris.uniroma1.it/handle/11573/1762124"
   ],
   "kg:openAccess": "yes",
   "isPartOf": {
    "@id": "venue/defensive-architecture-of-the-mediterranean-vol-xxii"
   },
   "kg:conference": {
    "name": "FORTMED 2026 – Fortification of the Mediterranean Coast",
    "location": "Rome, Lazio, Italy",
    "year": "2026"
   },
   "about": [
    {
     "@id": "keyword/fortifications"
    },
    {
     "@id": "keyword/historical-architecture"
    },
    {
     "@id": "keyword/reconstructive-drawing"
    },
    {
     "@id": "keyword/iconographic-analysis"
    }
   ],
   "kg:caseStudyScale": [
    {
     "@id": "scale/architectural"
    }
   ],
   "contentLocation": [
    {
     "@id": "place/verona-veneto-italy"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "publication/2026_Spallone_CarignanoHBIM",
   "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
   "identifier": "2026_Spallone_CarignanoHBIM",
   "name": "A Scan-to-HBIM Workflow to Trace the Level of Modelling Accuracy. The Case of Palazzo Carignano in Turin",
   "datePublished": "2026",
   "kg:publicationType": "Conference paper",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/spallone-roberta"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/vitali-marco"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/natta-fabrizio"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/bruschi-giovanni"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "Baroque architecture presents considerable morphological complexities relating to structural systems, distributive characteristics, and decorative elements. Palazzo Carignano in Turin, designed by Guarino Guarini from 1679, is a quintessential example of the period. The research addresses the challenge of documenting this complex building through integrated digital surveying and HBIM modeling of both structural and decorative systems. The Level of Accuracy (LOA) serves as a critical control parameter connecting the surveying and modeling phases, representing a central focus of this study on heritage documentation workflows.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "455-462",
   "issn": "2194-9034",
   "url": "https://isprs-archives.copernicus.org/articles/XLVIII-2-W12-2026/455/2026/",
   "volumeNumber": "XLVIII-2/W12-2026",
   "sameAs": [
    "https://doi.org/10.5194/isprs-archives-XLVIII-2-W12-2026-455-2026",
    "https://iris.uniroma1.it/handle/11573/1762132"
   ],
   "kg:openAccess": "yes",
   "kg:anvurScientificArea08": "yes",
   "kg:anvurClassA": "yes",
   "isPartOf": {
    "@id": "venue/international-archives-of-the-photogrammetry-remote-sensing-and-spatial-informat"
   },
   "kg:conference": {
    "name": "3DARCH 2026",
    "location": "Ancona, Marche, Italy",
    "year": "2026"
   },
   "about": [
    {
     "@id": "keyword/hbim"
    },
    {
     "@id": "keyword/level-of-accuracy"
