      "@id": "person/pini-agnese"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "Aquatic ecosystems have captured the interest of the international scientific community, spurring the development of new instruments and methodologies to explore, monitor, and preserve these environmental systems. The paper examines detecting submerged or semi-submerged objects using cameras positioned above water, a challenge in multimedia photogrammetry. Key obstacles include understanding refraction effects and extracting features under difficult optical conditions. The researchers conducted controlled tests at various water depths and turbulence levels to develop mathematical models accounting for optical distortion.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "129-136",
