  {
   "@id": "publication/2024_Russo_SantaCaterinaVerona",
   "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
   "identifier": "2024_Russo_SantaCaterinaVerona",
   "name": "Virtual reconstruction of destroyed fortifications: the case study of Santa Caterina in Verona",
   "datePublished": "2024",
   "kg:publicationType": "Conference paper",
   "author": {
    "@list": [
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-michele"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/flenghi-giulia"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/buonacucina-alessio"
     },
     {
      "@id": "person/russo-valentina"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "Military fortifications have always played a key role in territorial defense, with their location and visibility depending on strategic military choices and shape. The geometric development of these structures reflects centuries of refinement in construction techniques, warfare evolution, architectural consistency, and territorial adaptation. This research examines the Fort of Santa Caterina in Verona (Werk Hess), a fortification constructed between 1848 and 1856. Though only small traces remain today, the fort was architecturally significant due to its naturalistic environmental integration and dominant position as a perspective cornerstone of the fortified city. Through source analysis, territorial surveying, and representation techniques, the research provides a virtual reconstruction of this military structure.",
   "inLanguage": "ENG",
   "pagination": "603-610",
   "isbn": "9789928481405",
   "url": "http://ocs.editorial.upv.es/index.php/FORTMED/FORTMED2024/paper/view/18107",
