      "@id": "person/crespi-mattia"
     }
    ]
   },
   "abstract": "This research addresses multimedia photogrammetry for acquiring geometric data on submerged objects through external cameras. The team developed methods to model camera behavior in controlled environments using encoded targets and stereo-photogrammetry, testing the system's capacity to extract correct coordinates of images under varying water conditions. Their goal involves creating a predictive model for water refraction effects to enable accurate surveying of underwater cultural heritage in shallow water environments.",
